      "review_title": "",
      "review_description": "The sale process was well presented with an excellent and well informed representative.. But thats where it ends. Installation was a shambles with 56 holes left in the timber walls of the house, had 2 inverters installed which didn't line up and one was 30 odd mm higher than the other  . Conduit installed was damaged and silicone sealer smeared all over the walls. You can't paint over Silicon. One of the installers was ill when he arrived{didnt wear a mask}  and coughed and spat all over the yard, this was right in the height of COVID. They arrived without the needed government documentation to do the work during the covid lockdowns. They damaged plants in the garden and even when asked to take care they kept working where they caused the damage. There was plenty of room to work away from garden.Its been over 2 years since installation and despite consistent phone calls from myself the problem still hasnt been fixed despite numerous promises from them. They did send a person to fix the problem but he was clearly out of his depth and when i tried to speak to him about his work his response was that thats all he was going to do as HP ENERGY hadn't paid him. Funny when you consider that HP Energy demanded full payment when installation was done, even though not connected and knowing that there were several issues. They refused to connect installation to the grid until payment was done. We paid that day with promises from HP Energy that all issues would be fixed ASAP. do yourself a favour and stay away from HP Energy. Worst company I have ever dealt with.",
